#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100694 :question/id #uuid "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $CD$ is $2\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{C}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{D}=\\underset{2\\times2}{CD}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $C$ (blue) and column $1$ of $D$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{-4} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $C$ (blue) and column $2$ of $D$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & \\boxed{1} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $C$ (blue) and column $1$ of $D$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ \\boxed{-1} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $C$ (blue) and column $2$ of $D$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nCD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297 :topic/difficulty 0.9052140521889347 :topic/encompasse