256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b37a294-1d3c-567d-bf66-b3920a5fe9a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236585} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce9cddf-2413-5e15-89c7-45b259cab3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce9cddf-2413-5e15-89c7-45b259cab3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44f4bb4-30a2-5a30-959a-18587874cdc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237655}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53274149-3160-5be4-b6eb-415d49f449f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-1033" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthen $EF=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $EF$ is $2\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{4}}}}{E}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{4}}}\\times2}{F}=\\underset{2\\times2}{EF}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $E$ (blue) and column $1$ of $F$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{2} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $E$ (blue) and column $2$ of $F$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\boxed{18} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $E$ (blue) and column $1$ of $F$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ \\boxed{15} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $E$ (blue) and column $2$ of $F$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & \\boxed{9}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nEF=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7a62ec-13b8-543d-9616-121868053523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236016} {:answer/id #uuid "22e57d49-7fd7-563f-abb5-64190ff4aa02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236039} {:answer/id #uuid "24e7f5a9-a414-5f74-91fa-736878205105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236055} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9d6d90-f170-5014-9e02-b7a17b19bb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236497} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d5586-3d96-5a03-86a4-ba2ed71c39b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d5586-3d96-5a03-86a4-ba2ed71c39b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034} :answer-field/id #uuid "c96651e8-d8ed-5375-92a8-7fde59b35ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83b01661-23af-5f73-bcb3-22f2f416f38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1035" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $ST$ is $1\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{1\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{4}}}}{S}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{4}}}\\times2}{T}=\\underset{1\\times2}{ST}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $S$ (blue) and column $1$ of $T$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-3}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{6}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{24} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-3}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{6}} \\\\ &=24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $S$ (blue) and column $2$ of $T$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-3}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{red}{-2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{6}} & {\\color{red}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & \\boxed{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}})+({\\color{#4169E1}{-3}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nST=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d545a5-b2e6-5053-b8b6-37194c5c9aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263315} {:answer/id #uuid "338b8f0e-6e8c-5003-a20f-65d3696dd73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} {:answer/id #uuid "40cea55b-6167-57c5-a2d6-7f87677038d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263572} {:answer/id #uuid "53864c34-56a3-5553-afb8-033b263dcdea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263719} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bc1bd7-12d4-51d7-8d46-edc046b147b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338b8f0e-6e8c-5003-a20f-65d3696dd73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f084fe2-5f6e-5af3-b0dc-03f636f5e40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265467}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78f7d23e-60ed-507c-b4f6-6101bce65778" :question/math-academy-id "q-129495" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $AB$ is $2\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{A}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{B}=\\underset{2\\times2}{AB}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{6}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{-15} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}})+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{6}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &=-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{6}} & {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & \\boxed{3} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{6}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ \\boxed{-9} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{6}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{6}} & {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & \\boxed{10}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30980b36-8778-5a51-89b8-a81fc027883f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263413} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd13396-77b3-54fa-8ae9-6c7200fc84bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263533} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0eeffe-95e5-570e-9c36-aea6b4fd89db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264086} {:answer/id #uuid "975b44bb-df10-5292-a437-e855bf7bd551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264299} {:answer/id #uuid "aee8c241-2555-5612-b6c3-afa60e199249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30980b36-8778-5a51-89b8-a81fc027883f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263413} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f5a069b-5bd2-5270-9936-a86902646679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265502}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "910b9da2-b0da-578c-b6de-5df3df9fdc3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129496" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $XY$ is $1\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{1\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{X}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{Y}=\\underset{1\\times2}{XY}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $1$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{5}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{22} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ &=22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $2$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{5}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{2}} & {\\color{red}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & \\boxed{9}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nXY=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8b4b7ed-ec16-5051-9f0e-eb339152d483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 175921862986