nswer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642473}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94857107-c897-51f4-8aee-36e2b50b1efe" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $XY$ is $1\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{1\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{X}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{Y}=\\underset{1\\times2}{XY}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $1$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{-4}} & {\\color{gray}{-5}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{8} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&=({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-4}})+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-3}}) \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ &=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $2$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{-2}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{-4}} & {\\color{red}{-5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-3}} & {\\color{red}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\boxed{10}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&=({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-5}})+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nXY=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096dfddb-d40e-540c-a5e4-9ec9ea2ec7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -12 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642463} {:answer/id #uuid "27f18784-4500-57e7-95b1-512450bcdad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642465} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6e97b1-30f0-5cbb-982c-16a2416962a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642469} {:answer/id #uuid "c173493f-f21c-52a3-ba71-0f2173f2e025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642490} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b5eb28-c9cb-58ee-a0c5-a364992acce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c173493f-f21c-52a3-ba71-0f2173f2e025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642490} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f63b45f-39fc-55c1-a51b-567ea975b6ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b00e7f3e-2523-5d0a-a40a-274064ef9979" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $AB$ is $2\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{A}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{B}=\\underset{2\\times2}{AB}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{4}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-4}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{5}} & {\\color{gray}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{4} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-4}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{4}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-4}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{5}} & {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\boxed{8} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{4}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-4}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{-4}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{5}} & {\\color{gray}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-2}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ \\boxed{-10} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}})+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) \\\\ &=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{4}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{-4}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{5}} & {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-2}} & {\\color{red}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & \\boxed{-5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116d6830-b759-5827-938e-755cbdea6732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642464} {:answer/id #uuid "316b5c18-fb8b-556b-86bd-bf3f04f390b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642466} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8992e1-e263-5d99-a404-d8a59bf2c45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642474} {:answer/id #uuid "994a8143-199e-5a6d-98cf-c4b55e22c45d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642481} {:answer/id #uuid "e701046b-147e-5b94-94b1-06bffd5ad53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8992e1-e263-5d99-a404-d8a59bf2c45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642474} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c2850bf-b02f-541e-8bde-c32b146bae2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642477}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b95259cc-7f86-5c02-91ee-95e0cf893335" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthen $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $AB$ is $1\\times 3$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{1\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{2}}}}{A}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{2}}}\\times3}{B}=\\underset{1\\times3}{AB}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{5} & \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ &=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & \\boxed{5} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ &=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{13}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $3$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{red}{-1}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & \\boxed{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{13}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}})+{\\color{#4169E1}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"}]}
